# Migrations are checksum-governed: TOOLS/check-migration-ledger.mjs hashes the
# raw bytes of each .sql file and compares against a recorded checksum, and the
# 0039 reconstruction checksum is pinned to the Production ledger.
#
# On Windows, core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes
# those bytes and fails the ledger check on a file whose committed content is
# byte-identical to what Production expects. Forcing LF in the working tree
# makes the hash platform-independent instead of pinning a Windows-only value.
*.sql text eol=lf
